# TypeScript

- Give an exported function an explicit return type.
- Prefer `unknown` in a `catch` binding, then narrow it. Do not use `any`.
- A value that crosses a boundary (environment, request, file) is validated before the rest of the program trusts it.
- Model a closed set as a union of string literals, not an open `string`, when the callers must handle every case.
- Do not silence the compiler with a cast when a guard or a narrower type will do. A cast at a boundary needs a comment that says what was checked.

```ts
export function timeoutMs(value: unknown): number {
  if (typeof value !== "number" || value <= 0) throw new Error("Timeout must be a positive number.");
  return value;
}
```
